---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONSENT_MAX_AGE_MONTHS, DATA_CONTROLLER, POLICY_LAST_UPDATED, POLICY_VERSION } from '../../data/legal';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Prismatica" description="Prismatica privacy policy and GDPR information.">
	<main id="main-content" class="legal-page section-shell">
		<a href="/" class="legal-page__back" aria-label="Back to Prismatica">← Back to Prismatica</a>
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p><strong>Policy version:</strong> {POLICY_VERSION} · <strong>Last updated:</strong> {POLICY_LAST_UPDATED}</p>

		<nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
			<h2 class="legal-toc__title">Table of contents</h2>
			<ul class="legal-toc__list">
				<li><a href="#data-controller">Data controller</a></li>
				<li><a href="#data-collected">Data we collect and why</a></li>
				<li><a href="#retention">Retention</a></li>
				<li><a href="#storage-recipients">Where your data is stored and who receives it</a></li>
				<li><a href="#international-transfers">International transfers</a></li>
				<li><a href="#user-rights">Your rights</a></li>
				<li><a href="#is-providing-data-required">Is providing data required?</a></li>
				<li><a href="#automated-decisions">Automated decisions</a></li>
				<li><a href="#children">Children's privacy</a></li>
				<li><a href="#policy-changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
				<li><a href="#security">Data security</a></li>
				<li><a href="#cookies-tracking">Cookies and tracking</a></li>
				<li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
			</ul>
		</nav>

		<section>
			<h2 id="data-controller">Data controller</h2>
			<p>{DATA_CONTROLLER.name} is the data controller for Prismatica.</p>
			<p>Privacy contact: <a href={`mailto:${DATA_CONTROLLER.email}`}>{DATA_CONTROLLER.email}</a>.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="data-collected">Data we collect and why</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Account data:</strong> email address, username, password (stored only as a hash) and account timestamps. Used to create your account and sign you in. Legal basis: contract and legitimate interest in account security.</li>
				<li><strong>Preferences:</strong> theme and notification settings, and newsletter consent if you give it. Used to apply your settings. Legal basis: contract for service preferences and consent for optional communications.</li>
				<li><strong>Sessions and security logs:</strong> the IP address and browser user agent of each signed-in session, the IP address in the sign-in audit log, and timestamps. IP addresses are personal data. Used to keep you signed in and to secure your account. Legal basis: legitimate interest in security and fraud prevention.</li>
				<li><strong>Support and contact:</strong> the content of messages you send us. Used to answer you. Legal basis: legitimate interest and, where relevant, contract.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="retention">Retention</h2>
			<p>Account data is kept while your account is active. After you delete your account, data is erased or anonymised within one month, except where the law requires longer retention of specific records (for example security logs for a limited period).</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="storage-recipients">Where your data is stored and who receives it</h2>
			<p>Data is stored in self-hosted infrastructure operated by the Prismatica team. Processors may include email delivery and CAPTCHA providers strictly as needed to run the service. We do not sell personal data.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="international-transfers">International transfers</h2>
			<p>If a processor is outside the EEA, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses or an adequacy decision where applicable.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="user-rights">Your rights</h2>
			<p>Under the GDPR you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection where applicable.</p>
			<p>When signed in, you can download a machine-readable copy of your data, withdraw newsletter consent and request deletion of your account yourself on the <a href="/legal/data-rights/">Data Rights page</a>. For any other request, use the form on that page or contact <a href={`mailto:${DATA_CONTROLLER.email}`}>{DATA_CONTROLLER.email}</a>. We answer within one month; for complex requests this can be extended by two more months, and we will tell you why.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="is-providing-data-required">Is providing data required?</h2>
			<p>You need an email address, username and password to create an account. Optional fields and newsletter consent are not required to use the core service.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="automated-decisions">Automated decisions</h2>
			<p>Prismatica does not make decisions about you based solely on automated processing, including profiling, that produce legal or similarly significant effects. Anti-abuse checks such as rate limits and Cloudflare Turnstile only slow down or block suspicious sign-in attempts and can be retried.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="children">Children</h2>
			<p>The service is not intended for children under 15, the age of digital consent in France. We do not knowingly collect their data; if you believe a child has created an account, contact us and we will delete it.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="policy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>We may update this policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new policy on this page.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="security">Data security</h2>
			<p>Prismatica employs technical and organizational measures to protect personal data against accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure or access. All data is stored in self-hosted databases with access controls and encryption at rest.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="cookies-tracking">Cookies and tracking</h2>
			<p>The service uses a sign-in cookie and stores your preferences, consent choices and a workspace cache in your browser's local storage. It has no analytics or marketing scripts: the consent banner records your choice, and nothing else loads. See the <a href="/legal/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for the full list.</p>
			<button class="button button--ghost" type="button" data-manage-cookies aria-label="Manage cookie preferences">Manage cookie preferences</button>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
			<p>For privacy questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${DATA_CONTROLLER.email}`}>{DATA_CONTROLLER.email}</a>.</p>
		</section>

		<div class="legal-page__top-wrap"><a href="#main-content" class="legal-page__top-link">↑ Back to top</a></div>
	</main>
</Layout>
